From 870e4856924f583215f838ca9d17c93318a41a50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:38:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: IntersectionObserver delay skips only the target, not
 the observer

When a target's delay had not elapsed since its last update, the update
loop returned from the observer instead of continuing to the next target,
so every target registered after it went unprocessed. A target observed
while an earlier one was still inside its delay window got no initial
entry until the earlier one became eligible (in Chrome it is reported on
the next frame). The spec says to skip further processing for that target
only.
https://w3c.github.io/IntersectionObserver/#update-intersection-observations-algo

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../script/dom/intersectionobserver/intersectionobserver.rs     | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/script/dom/intersectionobserver/intersectionobserver.rs b/components/script/dom/intersectionobserver/intersectionobserver.rs
index f4d7d466e18..3e01b9b2f1b 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/intersectionobserver/intersectionobserver.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/intersectionobserver/intersectionobserver.rs
@@ -717,7 +717,7 @@ impl IntersectionObserver {
             if time - registration.last_update_time.get() <
                 Duration::from_millis(self.delay.get().max(0) as u64)
             {
-                return;
+                continue;
             }
 
             // Step 3
